        "original_id": "9740e6fb-4683-56be-b54c-a8b12b739e26",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Monfragüe, Doñana National Park, Andalusia, Spain, Huelva, Seville\n- Organizations: World Wildlife Fund, Spanish government\n- Topics: national parks, nature reserves, bird-life, marsh conservation\n\nFacts:\n- In 1969, Doñana National Park was established as a nature reserve when the World Wildlife Fund joined with the Spanish government and purchased a section of marshes to protect it.\n- Monfragüe, also called Parque Nacional Monfragüe in Spanish, is a Spanish national park noted for its bird-life.\n- Doñana National Park is a natural reserve in Andalusia in southern Spain, and most of its territory is in Huelva province while the rest is in Seville province.",
